      "title": "Why it matters",
      "body": "Hotel staff usually need one concrete detail: your booking, room number, time, or the item you need. For \"I'd like to check in\", the useful move is putting the need first and leaving room for the helper to confirm the detail. Pause after the phrase so the person can confirm before you add more words.",
